<title>AUSTRALIA: TENNIS-AUSTRALIAN OPEN MEN'S AND WOMEN'S SEEDS. [CORRECTED 9:25 GMT]</title>
<headline>TENNIS-AUSTRALIAN OPEN MEN'S AND WOMEN'S SEEDS. [CORRECTED 9:25 GMT]</headline>
<dateline>MELBOURNE 1997-01-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>List of seeded players announced on Thursday for the Australian Open tennis tournament beginning at Melbourne Park on Monday (figure in brackets denotes current world ranking).</p>
<p>Men's singles:</p>
<p>1-Pete Sampras (U.S., 1)</p>
<p>2-Michael Chang (U.S., 2)</p>
<p>3-Goran Ivanisevic (Croatia, 3)</p>
<p>4-Yevgeny Kafelnikov (Russia, 4)</p>
<p>5-Thomas Muster (Austria, 5)</p>
<p>6-Boris Becker (Germany, 6)</p>
<p>7-Thomas Enqvist (Sweden, 9)</p>
<p>8-Wayne Ferreira (South Africa, 10)</p>
<p>(Corrects rankings for Enqvist and Ferreira)</p>
<p>9-Marcelo Rios (Chile, 11)</p>
<p>10-Albert Costa (Spain, 13)</p>
<p>11-Jim Courier (U.S., 15)</p>
<p>12-Magnus Gustafsson (Sweden, 16)</p>
<p>13-Jan Siemerink (Netherlands, 17)</p>
<p>14-Felix Mantilla (Spain, 18)</p>
<p>15-Michael Stich (Germany, 19)</p>
<p>16-Alberto Berasategui (Spain, 20)</p>
<p>Women's singles:</p>
<p>1-Steffi Graf (Germany, 1)</p>
<p>2-Arantxa Sanchez Vicario (Spain, 3)</p>
<p>3-Conchita Martinez (Spain, 4)</p>
<p>4-Martina Hingis (Switzerland, 6)</p>
<p>5-Anke Huber (Germany, 7)</p>
<p>6-Iva Majoli (Croatia, 8)</p>
<p>7-Lindsay Davenport (U.S., 9)</p>
<p>8-Irina Spirlea (Romania, 10)</p>
<p>9-Karina Habsudova (Slovakia, 11)</p>
<p>10-Brenda Schultz-McCarthy (Netherlands, 12)</p>
<p>11-Judith Wiesner (Austria, 13)</p>
<p>12-Amanda Coetzer (South Africa, 14)</p>
<p>13-Elena Likhovtseva (Russia, 16)</p>
<p>14-Mary Joe Fernandez (U.S., 17)</p>
<p>15-Chanda Rubin (U.S., 18)</p>
<p>16-Sabine Appelmans (Belgium, 19).</p>
